# Project

Kaggle Titanic competition solution. Python, managed with uv (pyproject.toml, not requirements.txt). Run scripts with `uv run`.

# Commit messages

- lowercase only, including the first word
- minimalistic: a single short line in imperative mood, e.g. "add omegaconf config", "fix fare imputation"
- no trailing period, no conventional-commit prefixes (feat:, fix:), no co-author trailers
- body only when the why isn't obvious from the diff

# Code style

- keep it simple; no over-engineering
- docstrings for public functions, no comments narrating obvious code
